~ start

Willy: Where the hell is that seed? You can't see nothing out here! They boxed in the whole goddamn neighborhood!

Biff: There are people all around here. Don't you realize that?

Willy: I'm busy, don't bother me.

Biff: I'm saying goodbye to you, Pop.

Willy: You're not going to see Oliver tomorrow?

Biff: I've got no appointment, dad.

Willy: He put his arm around you, and you've got no appointment?

Biff: Pop, get this now will you?
Biff: Every time I've left it's been a fight that sent me out of here. Today I realize something about myself and I tried to explain it to you and I...
Biff: I think I'm just not smart enough to make any sense out of it for you.
Biff: To hell with whose fault it is or anything like that. Let's just wrap it up, heh?
Biff: Come on in, and we'll tell Mom.

Willy: No... no... I don't want to see her.

Biff: What do you mean, you don't want to see her? You don't want them calling you yellow, do you?
=> END